### Nodejs
One of the aspects, for nodejs mostly used is Networking, provides already built in methods using using which can able raise or accept the network call, so it can act as a clint aw well as server (if that netwok, return the response)
- So in this, process of creating the project we would how it  will work as the server. So ham bahut baar server bana rahe honge lakin kuchh logg directly, batate hain ki, express, next, etc use karke server bana lete hain hai lakin yaha ham khud server banayenge. Ye library sirf hamara kaam asaan karti hai. 

### How can you actually write a server in a node js?
- Firsltly creates the index.js file
- Nodejs provids you the http module, http module help in doing the all type of http interation. 
- so we are requiring it for the use it means it is the core module of the nodejs, basically we do not need to install it or manage it. 
- How network interation work, two machine have interact with each other, one act as clint and on act as server, if the client want request the server, then it must know the ip adress of the serever, and they also need to know the port no of at which the actually server process is happening. Ip + port = Socket address. 
- so ham yaha apne brawser se request karenge, apne nodejs server par. So we are having the both brawser and server in my machine , technically we can replace the ip address part with localhost, so if they are on same machine then we do need to gave any ip address. 
- CreateServer() :- So ye fun ek call back function expect karta hai, aur wo call back function jya expext  karta hai? So this is the call back fn we use to create the server, and create server method is reposible to call this call back function. 
 - So ab agar koi hamko request bhejta hai then ham kuchh toh reply karenge. Us request ke sath kya karna hai, wo sab is call bacj fun mai excute karenge. 
 - this call back fn accept two object req, res, aur koi chiz aa rahi hai then usko req object configure karega if koi chize ko bhejna hai usko res object  handle or configure karega. 
 - res object ke pass ek method hai write, we can pass string,json,stringify string anything. 
 - we need to use res.end so we need to end respose to ensure that request is complete or not. 

 So this is the basic server, we have been created. So agar complex project par kaam kar rahe honge then aise bahut saare req and res object ke aur bhi methods ko use kar rahe honge, matlab project ke according apna server bana sakte hai. 

- Abhi tak toh ham apne server bana chuke hai, then how we are going to start the server. So server object ke pass ek method hota hai listen() method.
Listen(): Expect:- take PORT, and callback fn
 - this callback fn will be runing when server is succesfully listening and running

- So abhi toh server aur client same hai, lakin idle case mai aisa nahi hota hai, server kisi machine par chal raha hota hai, aur client duniya mai kahi bhi ho sakta hai. 
- When client and server are on the same machine then we donot need the internet, so the client and server can interact, so when server run on another machine, then we need internet. 
- Then when we are working in the company there is the highly chances that we do not use http module to set up the server because  it can do everything but it cannot provide the ease of the use case, there are framework and libary which make server writing the code much easy and wonderful that what we want, our aganda is to make product, we donot want to go in much more complexity. 
   - for  that we have the framwork express.js , good community support, good documentation, we can find  the any  type of solution on stackoverflow, linkdin, github, etc. 
   
### How using the expressjs we are going to write the server? 
so we were developing the photosharing type of application, append some photo, share the link of the photo. So we will be seeing how we can setup the http server in node js using express js. Expressjs functions uses internally the http nodejs module. 
  - Es6 enabling -> add type property to the package.json : for the import and export functionality
  - imort express from "express" yaha jo express hai wo ek funnction hai. 
  - aur jab ham is function ko call karte hai then it return the server object

- In the plain server we are able to set/configure that when req comes then what to do and what to response. then is approch mai server ko set up karne ke liye yaha kasie karenge. As this going to be the http server, every http request is going to have a lind of http methods like get, delete, post, etc. 
  - so we can call , like app.get(), and we can pass to parameter string and callback.So we can define on every tpye of http request, what to do with get type of request. 
  - Lakin plain-server mai hamare pass ek he call back function tha aur hamko ek call back mai define karte the ki hamko kya karna hai on / , /ping, etc
  - ab yaha jab request kisi specific url ke liye aayegi then uske liye specificallly callback run hogi. 
    - req :-  incoming http request
    - res :- to be outgoing the http response 
    we can send the different type of response. 

    - verifying the post  request in the plain server using javascript, so we can go through inspect-> console-> write basic function or async type and here request the post request. -> fatch("url", {method : POST})
    - You can go to the documentation, how to do post request with fetch api -> approch. 
    - 2nd approch hai html form kr through post request karna as form have the property, action/method. this action define the url on which you want to submit the form.

- There is also different http methods such as  :- put, delete, how can we raise the request on this type, again javascript is useful. In similarly. 
- using brawser url, we are only able to do the get request. 
- Html form allow only to do the get and post request, it doesnot allow another http method like delete, put, etc. 

- so ham har baar toh request brawser ke console mai jakar js ke through method nahi call karenge as it bahut jayda waste of time ho jayega. So there are many developer tool some of them is postman. 

Postman ki bahut saari functialities ke baare mai pad rahe honge. Dekho poject banate smaay ham bahut saari api call kar rahe honge like 100 of api, for everey api, i have to write the base address, for every api. If by chances we have to change the port no then we have to go all api we have to change the address. For that postman gives the, variables, inside a collection and we can use inside the request. 
  - Creating a variable in postman. 
- There is lot of alternative of postman. 

### Connect the mongoDB to our project
- We need two things to connect with mongodb instances 1. URL of the instance to connect with as we are going to connect the different server. 2. mongoDb libarary , need a libaray which have the all logic to connect with mongoDB. Nodejs has different libaray by which we connect to the mongodb instance. So we have the mongoDb driver through which we can able to connect with the mongoDB instances. 
Steps are :- 
  1. First require the MongoClient from the MongoDB
  2. Const URL set karo
  3. Then is url ko pass kardo MongoClient mai and usko store karlo client const mai
  4. Then is instance jo client hai usko client.connect() call kardo

  There are also set of libaray which we call as ORM(Object Relational Mapper) and ODM(Object Document Mapper) , both are same, only the difference is ORM is relational DB and ODM is for the Document DB.  The puspose as developers we are more found of class based code,etc. 
   - These libary provides us the function which we can directly use, we do not need to write raw querries. The ORM and ODM libaray , internally converts these as an querries. 
   1. Write our own server logic
   2. Then call the ODM functions 
   3. The ODM will convert it into the querries. 

   Most famous ODM for mongoDB is mongoose/prisma/,etc

   So we can follow some basic steps to connect the mongoDB with mongoose. 
   1. Require
   2. Call using the async await using mongoose instance , connect. 